            <ArticleTitle>Concerns and choices in general practice.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Osteoarthritis is a common problem in general practice and a major indication for NSAIDs. Many patients with osteoarthritis are elderly and therefore particularly at risk from adverse reactions. Co-morbidity and co-prescription may lead to drug interactions. For these reasons, safe NSAIDs are the first choice for this disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
